          "toolId": "copilot_runInTerminal"
        },
        {
          "value": "Great! The Android SDK configuration is now working correctly. The error message has changed from \"Failed to resolve the Android SDK path\" to \"No Android connected device found\", which means the SDK is properly detected.\n\n## Next Steps\n\nYou now need to either:\n\n### Option A: Connect a Physical Android Device\n1. Connect your Android phone/tablet via USB\n2. Enable Developer Options and USB Debugging on your device\n3. Run `adb devices` to verify the device is detected\n4. Run `bunx expo run:android` again\n\n### Option B: Create an Android Emulator\nLet me help you create an Android emulator. We'll need to use the Android SDK tools: ",
          "supportThemeIcons": false,
          "supportHtml": false,
          "baseUri": {
            "$mid": 1,
            "path": "/home/junior/Projects/ecodreum/ecodreum-app/",
            "scheme": "file"
          }
        },
        {
          "kind": "prepareToolInvocation",
          "toolName": "copilot_runInTerminal"
        },
        {
          "kind": "toolInvocationSerialized",
          "invocationMessage": "Using \"Run In Terminal\"",
          "isConfirmed": true,
          "isComplete": true,
          "toolSpecificData": {
            "kind": "terminal",
            "language": "sh",
            "command": "~/Android/Sdk/cmdline-tools/latest/bin/avdmanager create avd -n \"Expo_Emulator\" -k \"system-images;android-36;google_apis_playstore;x86_64\" -d \"pixel_7\""
          },
          "toolCallId": "1fcde368-3291-4791-8bea-7accea15a213",
          "toolId": "copilot_runInTerminal"
        },
        {
          "value": "It looks like the command-line tools aren't installed. Let's check what tools are available: ",
